&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As VP, Global FP&amp;amp;A, you will be a strategic finance leader and operating partner to the CFO, CEO, and Executive Leadership Team, responsible for company-wide planning, forecasting, performance management, and decision support as we scale a multi-product, multi-region SaaS business. You will translate operational performance into financial outcomes, establish an executive-ready KPI operating cadence, and elevate resource allocation decisions to maximize durable growth and capital efficiency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead analysis to define financial objectives and KPIs that drive accountability and performance for our cross-functional, matrixed organization across multiple regions, product lines, and go-to-market motions. You will also support strategic initiatives related to M&amp;amp;A, investments, and optimization. This role is for someone who is highly motivated to transform and lead a global FP&amp;amp;A function and dynamic team that will enable our growth aspirations beyond $1B revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a core strategic advisor to the CFO and executive team, influencing decisions on growth, investment tradeoffs, operating leverage, and long-range value creation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In partnership with the executive team, establish a strategic roadmap and growth targets for all business lines and geographies, including KPIs to drive business performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the long-range plan (LRP), translating strategy into measurable financial targets, investment guardrails, and capacity plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver clear executive narratives on performance and outlook; present insights and recommendations to the CEO, CFO, and Board.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Annual Operating Plan, rolling forecasts, and scenario modeling across all regions and functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive transformation of planning models to improve forecast accuracy and speed of decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop SaaS operating models and KPI dashboards connecting leading indicators to ARR and revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Institutionalize KPI governance, business review cadences, and corrective action loops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver variance analyses and insights tied to strategic outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales, Marketing, and Customer Success on bookings, revenue, retention, and capacity planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive ROI-based resource allocation and investment prioritization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide financial rigor on pricing, deal economics, and margin impacts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product and Engineering to align roadmap investments with financial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own R&amp;amp;D headcount and expense planning with a focus on efficiency and ROI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploy scalable planning systems to support technical organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead financial evaluation of strategic investments and M&amp;amp;A opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In partnership with Corporate Development, develop valuation, synergy, and post-deal performance tracking models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support capital efficiency and cash flow outlooks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce Board-ready financial reporting with clear insights and action orientation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner across Finance to support earnings, forecasting, and reporting cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide credible guidance and strategic context to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own FP&amp;amp;A process optimization, automation, and systems modernization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve speed, accuracy, and scalability of forecasts and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a single source of truth for metrics and assumptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor future finance leaders and evolve org design to match scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Qualifications&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of progressive FP&amp;amp;A or strategic finance experience in a scaling SaaS environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of SaaS metrics, operating models, and value drivers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional modeling, analytical, and executive communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven leader with experience building and scaling global teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA, CPA, CFA, or other advanced credential preferred but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel domestically and internationally as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;The Salary Range for this role is &lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;$240,000 - $320,000&lt;/span&gt;. At AvePoint, we strive to offer competitive, fair, and equitable total rewards. The listed salary range represents a good faith estimate, with final offers based on location, experience, skills, and qualifications. The listed range reflects base salary only; our total rewards include base salary, comprehensive benefits (medical, dental, vision, 401(k) with match, unlimited PTO), and depending on the role, bonuses, commissions, or equity (RSUs). We welcome compensation discussions—apply even if your expectations fall outside the range.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ui-provider a b c d e f g h i j k l m n o p q r s t u v w x y z ab ac ae af ag ah ai aj ak&quot;&gt;Any personal data you share with us during the application process will be processed strictly in compliance with applicable data protection laws and our &lt;a id=&quot;menur12n&quot; class=&quot;fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn&quot; href=&quot;https://www.avepoint.com/company/privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

techaviv-betterhelp:greenhouse:422177400.descriptionHtml:
&lt;p&gt;UpLift &amp;amp; BetterHelp – Redefining Access to Mental Healthcare&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At UpLift, we believe mental health is just as important as physical health — and we&#39;re rethinking the mental healthcare model. UpLift is a multi-sided marketplace, applying technology to empower patients to find Therapists and Psychiatric providers covered by their insurance plan.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While 1 in 5 Americans struggle with mental health issues, only 40% of this group received care in the last year. At the same time, only 30% of therapists accept insurance. UpLift acts as the bridge between patient, provider, and insurer — empowering patients to find the best care for their needs at a price they can afford.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join UpLift&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible earnings model*:&lt;/strong&gt; Compensation includes both patient care and collaboration activities. Physicians can also earn $30 per completed chart review. Total monthly earnings may vary based on state coverage and activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expand access to care:&lt;/strong&gt; Provide psychiatric services to individuals who otherwise may not have access to mental healthcare.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative model:&lt;/strong&gt; Support and supervise Nurse Practitioners (NPs) through formal collaboration agreements, including chart reviews and consultation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;All-in-one virtual platform:&lt;/strong&gt; Focus on your patients — UpLift handles credentialing, enrollment, and platform operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work from anywhere:&lt;/strong&gt; This role is 100% remote, with care delivered via UpLift’s purpose-built telemedicine platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible commitment:&lt;/strong&gt; Part-time, 1099 contract position with autonomy over your clinical schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct video consultations and communicate with patients via telemedicine.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess, diagnose, and treat patients, including prescribing medication when clinically appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide supervision and oversight to Nurse Practitioners (NPs) in states requiring collaborative agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete required chart reviews and provide timely consultation support to NPs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain responsiveness for collaboration duties in accordance with state requirements and UpLift standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate care with UpLift’s network of therapists and other providers to ensure high-quality outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide empathetic, evidence-based care while upholding UpLift’s clinical and service standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share product and workflow feedback with UpLift’s engineering and operations teams to help improve care delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Board-certified Psychiatrist with active clinical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active and unrestricted medical license(s) in one or more of the following priority states: Virginia, Texas, Florida, Georgia, or North Carolina.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-state licensure strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supervising or collaborating with Psychiatric Nurse Practitioners (e.g. NPs) is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable prescribing medication when clinically appropriate and permitted by state law.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled at using online tools and technology to deliver virtual care.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and ability to provide timely consultation support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous telemedicine experience is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Important to Know&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a part-time, contract (1099) position — not a salaried employee role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Physicians may set their own schedules for patient care; however, collaboration responsibilities require ongoing responsiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Physicians may stop seeing patients at any time, but collaborative agreement responsibilities require a 120-day wind-down period to ensure continuity of care.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compensation structure varies by state depending on collaboration requirements (capped vs. uncapped states).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;UpLift will credential and enroll you with multiple health plans to expand access to insured patients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All care is delivered remotely through UpLift’s telehealth platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All clinical decisions are made independently by licensed providers in accordance with state telehealth laws and professional standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;License/Certification:&lt;/strong&gt; Medical License (Required)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Pennsylvania&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Remote&lt;/p&gt;
